An archetype, not a replica
---------------------------

This cartridge models a FAMILY: an upright slab with a screen above its
controls. It models no manufacturer's product. It draws no logo, wordmark,
badge, glyph, colourway, texture, vent or parting line, and no outline or
control arrangement was traced or measured from a device.

The two presets are ILLUSTRATIVE. Their names describe a size and a layout, and
their dimensions are round numbers chosen to show the parameter space. They are
not the dimensions of any device.

The input event names in the manifest's `device` block (BTN_SOUTH, ABS_X,
KEY_POWER and so on) are the names the Linux kernel gives input events. They are
the interface a program and a driver agree on, and they are used here as names.
